_cents` used `int(amount * 100)`, which truncates. In binary floating point, `19.99 * 100` is `1998.9999\u2026`, so it returned 1998 instead of 1999. The same truncation made `0.29` give 28 cents and `4.35` give 434, so the other two failures had the same cause.\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now converts through `Decimal(str(amount))` and rounds half up to whole cents.\n\nI didn't change `discounts.py` or `tax.py`. The rounding in `apply_percent` and `tax_cents` was already correct.\n\n`to_cents` rounds the decimal form of the float, so `19.995` becomes 2000 cents. If you'd rather reject amounts with more than two decimal places, that would be a separate change.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 97748, "requests_cache_write": 28478, "requests_cost_usd": 0.0999178, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1892, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial8", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 15, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T23:14:03.701377+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 18.133, "t_checker_s": 0.326, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1906, "tokens_cache_read": 97748, "tokens_cache_write": 28478, "tokens_fresh": 1906, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_cache_read": 97748, "tokens_main_cache_write": 28478, "tokens_main_calls": 6, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_output": 1892, "tokens_output": 1892, "tokens_proxy_cache_